      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-02-01T23:43:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If I wrote the rules correctly, you need to flip the Bear before the Chairman emerges; the Chairman's inherent flip requires Underbosses to be in the trash, and this prevents that from happening and provides an alternative in which the Chairman flips when the Bear dies.&nbsp;</p><p>The chain would be: The Bear acts as though he was Underbosses, and gets beaten down while summoning thugs. Once you've beaten him enough, he flips, the Chairman flips, and suddenly the Chairman has hired a set of Underbosses who drop into play to fight. Then you beat the Chairman the old-fashioned way.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:20.992Z",
