      "id": 214211,
      "name": "Magpie",
      "username": "Magpie",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/magpie/{size}/1864_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-02-08T10:22:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>What about the prison breaks? Agent of Gloom has you discard any lab raids that come up, and then dealing damage. Maybe \"Whenever a prison break would be played, discard it instead and restore the operative to full health.\" In this way the effect of prison break is maintained, by refreshing/prolonging the lifespan of the underboss effects.</p><p>Strictly speaking, you would need a variant card for the chairman that said to put the operative into play, \"the bear\" side up, instead of \"assassin\" side up.</p><p>Another thing that occured to me: The Contract has an end of turn attack, while the other underbosses only have their thug-pull as end of turn effect. Just an observation.</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
